# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AWS Credentials for Bootstrap
#
# SINGLE-ACCOUNT setup:
#   cp aws-credentials.example aws-credentials
#   Fill in your temporary credentials.
#
# MULTI-ACCOUNT setup (one file per environment):
#   cp aws-credentials.example aws-credentials.dev
#   cp aws-credentials.example aws-credentials.staging
#   cp aws-credentials.example aws-credentials.prod
#   Fill each file with credentials for the corresponding AWS account.
#
# All aws-credentials* files are gitignored — they never leave your machine.
#
# These should be TEMPORARY credentials (SSO session or STS assume-role).
# They expire automatically. Never use long-lived IAM user keys.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
AWS_SESSION_TOKEN=
